GREP(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    grep - search text with regular expressions

SYNOPSIS
    grep [-EFinvclrhHw] pattern [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints matching lines. Patterns are basic regular expressions by default;
    -E selects extended expressions and -F matches a fixed string. -i ignores
    case, -n prints line numbers, -v inverts selection, -c prints counts,
    -l prints matching filenames, -w requires whole words. -r recursively
    searches directories; it follows symbolic links named as operands and
    skips those it finds while descending. -h hides filenames; -H always
    shows them.
    A file named - means standard input. -- ends options. Matching text is
    red on capable terminals. Exit status: 0 matches, 1 none, 2 an error.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
